Subject: [PATCH 31/38] =?UTF-8?q?feat(qwen3-tts):=20shared-engine=20ctors?=
 =?UTF-8?q?=20=E2=80=94=20slot=20pool=20reuses=20deserialized=20engine=20w?=
 =?UTF-8?q?eights=20(re-port=20a361221+21119ec,=20spec=20#6)?=
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

EngineExecutor: new createForLLMBorrowed(engine, cfg) factory + private
borrowed-engine ctor. Creates only a fresh per-instance kUSER_MANAGED
execution context off a live ICudaEngine owned by another executor (no
IRuntime, no re-deserialize). All engine introspection routed through
enginePtr(); getEnginePtr() exposes the engine for sharing. Owner must
outlive borrowers; per-instance context/graph-cache stay private.

Code2WavRunner: same borrowed-engine ctor (context + activation memory +
I/O buffers per instance; engine weights shared) + getEnginePtr().

Qwen3OmniTTSRuntime: shared-engine ctor taking borrowed Talker +
CodePredictor engines; ctor body extracted into initializeRuntime() and
initializeEngineRunners() picks the borrowed factory when set. Non-engine
assets (tokenizer, MLP weights, embedding tables) stay per-instance.

Worker: slots 1..N-1 construct via the shared ctors off slot 0 (covers all
three engines: talker/code_predictor/code2wav). EDGE_LLM_TTS_SHARED_ENGINE=0
opts back into independent per-slot deserialization (memory A/B baseline).
destroySlotPool now frees slots in reverse so borrowers die before the owner.
Default max_slots=1 path is untouched (slot 0 always uses the path ctors).

